From eff02c89fe113b6f08ea7bbf20cafb1103376a7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:01:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/51] Replace the fixed background modes with an opacity
 slider and add original-text dimming

The style editor used to offer three fixed background modes
(translucent black, solid black, none). Following what mainstream
players do (Android system captions, VLC), the solid background now
has a continuous opacity slider (0-100%), and the original-language
layer gets its own opacity control (30-100%) so the translation can
stand out, like bilingual subtitle browser extensions do.

- BisubStyle: retire BG_TRANSLUCENT/BG_OPAQUE and the two hardcoded
  color constants; keep BG_NONE and add BG_SOLID with
  DEFAULT_BACKGROUND_OPACITY (0.5) and DEFAULT_ORIGINAL_ALPHA (1.0)
- BisubPrefs: Style gains backgroundOpacity and originalAlpha;
  loadStyle migrates the retired modes 0/1 to BG_SOLID with 50%/100%
  opacity, so existing users keep the look they had
- BisubSubtitleView: the background block alpha comes from the style;
  the original layer (outline included) fades as a whole
- style editor: two radio buttons (solid/none), an opacity slider
  that disables itself while no background is selected, and an
  original-text opacity slider; drop the now-unused traditional
  provider summary strings left over from the field-hiding patch
